# URLs the link checker (lychee) skips, one regular expression per line.
# Add a URL here only when it cannot be checked without a login or from a CI runner, and say why.
# A link that is simply broken gets fixed, not ignored.

# Local servers in examples (the figma-console bridge, MCP servers on this machine).
^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)([:/]|$)

# Figma Community pages answer 403 to non-browser clients and 200 to a browser (checked 2026-10-05).
^https://www\.figma\.com/community/

# LinkedIn answers 999 to non-browser clients, so a CI runner cannot check it (checked 2026-10-05).
^https://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/
